**Blocking: catch export-iterator failures on nonzero ranks.** Build an export plan, disable one of its weight quantizers, then collectively call this API with the stale plan. [prepare_modelopt_export_tasks](https://github.com/NVIDIA-NeMo/Megatron-Bridge/blob/ffb916da9ecbb556471ffc70d1b54ae03744b962/src/megatron/bridge/models/conversion/modelopt_utils.py#L810-L828) raises the validation error on every rank. Rank zero catches it and enters the final broadcast, but nonzero ranks escape this unguarded loop without entering that broadcast. If callers catch this expected rejection and keep the process group alive, rank zero hangs/times out instead of every rank receiving the failure. The existing [distributed stale-plan assertion](https://github.com/NVIDIA-NeMo/Megatron-Bridge/blob/ffb916da9ecbb556471ffc70d1b54ae03744b962/tests/unit_tests/models/test_modelopt_utils.py#L933-L936) covers the underlying validation, not this wrapper.

**Correction:** replace the nonzero branch and final status broadcast with guarded consumption and a common error exchange:
```python
        else:
            try:
                for _ in tensors:
                    pass
            except Exception as exception:
                error = f"{type(exception).__name__}: {exception}"

        if dist.is_initialized():
            errors = [None] * dist.get_world_size()
            dist.all_gather_object(errors, error)
            error = "; ".join(dict.fromkeys(item for item in errors if item)) or None
```
Keep the final `RuntimeError` and rank-zero draining behavior. The invariant is that a collectively rejected export reaches the same terminal status exchange on every rank.

**Preservation / acceptance:** proposed two-rank Gloo regression: invalidate a supplied plan and assert both ranks finish with the validation error under a bounded timeout. Also inject a rank-zero shard-write failure while tensors remain: all ranks must finish consuming the stream and receive that write error. Successful exports must still write only on rank zero and return on every rank. Retain the existing stale-plan rejection assertion. This suggested change was source-traced, not executed; verify before adoption.

